# Hard bugs and repro

Default for features and straightforward edits: implement, `scripts/check.sh`,
review, commit. Use this when the bug is unclear, a fix already failed once
(rule 6), or the maintainer asks for a repro test or Debug Mode.

## Maintainer shortcuts

- **@ files** — When the maintainer @-mentions paths, start there. Widen the
  search only if those files are not enough.
- **Debug Mode (Shift+Tab)** — State a hypothesis, measure (probe skill or
  logcat), ask for on-device reproduction when needed, then one targeted fix.
  No speculative edits before something is measured.

## Which path

| Situation | First step |
|---|---|
| JVM logic in BTLib (aliases, parsing, settings helpers) | `.cursor/skills/extract-then-test`: failing test from requirement or observation, then fix |
| UI, binder, threads, Lua, symptom only on phone | `.cursor/skills/probe` or logcat; device-test card after `scripts/deploy.sh` |
| Typo, copy, guard script, docs-only | No repro ritual |

One measurement pass per hypothesis — do not duplicate probe logging and Debug
Mode instrumentation for the same guess.

Rule 5 still applies: the test expectation comes from the requirement or from
what was observed, not from the method you are about to change.